WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.101
- You ready?
- Oh yeah.

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:02.768
[music playing]
[thud]

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:03.502
[cracking]

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:03.970
[popping]

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:04.704
 It will--

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:05.438
[clanging]

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:08.008 line:14%
[music playing]

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.510
 Attila the Hun's
Sword of Mars.

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:12.311
[laughter]

00:00:12.378 --> 00:00:14.147
 Whoa.

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:14.780
 Yes.

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:16.015
[clang]

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.150
NARRATOR: Known as
the scourge of God,

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.183
Attila the Hun was
one of the most

00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:19.652
feared conquerors in history.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:21.221
[music playing]

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:23.256
The leader of the Hunnic Empire,
his group of nomadic tribes

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.557
wreaked havoc across Europe
during the fifth century.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:26.393
[battle cries]

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:27.460
[swords clanging]

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.095
Though he was once a
great ally to them,

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:30.897
he plagued Roman territories,
sacking major cities

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.399
like Constantinople.

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:34.434
Legend states that Attila
was given the Sword of Mars

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.302
by a herdsman,
fulfilling a prophecy,

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:39.105
and a direct sign from
the Roman war god, Mars,

00:00:39.172 --> 00:00:40.606
of his divine rule.

00:00:40.673 --> 00:00:42.776
The lethal weapon featured
a curved handle with a spear

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:45.812
point tip that gave it
exceptional control, allowing

00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:47.380
for accurate and brutal thrust.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.916
After Attila's death
in the year 453,

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:51.918
the Hunnic Empire
quickly dissolved.

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:54.087
However, the story of
Attila's many conquests

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:56.022
still live on through the
television miniseries,

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:56.923
"Attila."

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:58.525
 All right, bladesmiths.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.593
To find out what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:03.863
I will deliver killing blows
on this ballistics dummy.

00:01:03.929 --> 00:01:05.131
Randy, you're up first.
Are you ready?

00:01:05.197 --> 00:01:06.566
- I am.
- Let's do this.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:08.501
[music playing]

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:09.468
[cutting]

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:12.539
[music playing]

00:01:13.906 --> 00:01:16.776
[chopping]

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:20.213
[music playing]

00:01:20.846 --> 00:01:22.115
 Nice.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:25.718
[music playing]

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:31.558
[laughter]

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:32.659
 All right, Randy.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.360
Let's talk about your
Sword of Mars here.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.596
First up, the Damascus pattern
you have here is gorgeous.

00:01:37.696 --> 00:01:38.998
 Thank you.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:41.134
 The weapon design is very
aggressive for thrusting

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:42.335
and slashing.

00:01:42.401 --> 00:01:43.937
Now, your handle construction.

00:01:44.003 --> 00:01:46.906
If you reverse this,
it'll be easier to have

00:01:47.006 --> 00:01:48.407
something to lock on to.

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:50.009
The fact that the
flare is right here,

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:53.713
forcing my hand to open up if
I want to marry into the hilt.

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:55.181
This is a very sharp weapon.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:58.918
The tip pierces all the way
through, cuts on the way

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:02.621
out, it's pointy and
scary, and it will KEAL.

00:02:02.688 --> 00:02:03.556
 Thank you.

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:04.090
 Good job.

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:05.057
 All right, Dan.

00:02:05.124 --> 00:02:06.024
It is your turn.
You ready?

00:02:06.091 --> 00:02:06.793
 Hell yeah.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.094
 Let's do this.

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:09.061
 I was hoping the kill
test would be a dummy.

00:02:09.161 --> 00:02:10.897
I know heads will roll.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.631
[music playing]

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:16.035
[cutting]

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:18.571
[music playing]

00:02:18.671 --> 00:02:21.940
[chopping]

00:02:22.041 --> 00:02:25.545
[music playing]

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:36.789
 All right, Dan, let's
talk about your weapon here.

00:02:36.890 --> 00:02:38.591
I love the balance
of your blade.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:42.328
When I go forward, it's
not hard to pull back to go

00:02:42.395 --> 00:02:43.730
in again for another KEAL.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.164
Now, your handle construction.

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.199
It's curved enough
to where it doesn't

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:48.500
want to fly out of my hand.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:50.269
It's got a good grip
and control for this.

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:53.873
Your edge allows for very
deep cuts into the abdomen

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.441
right there.

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:58.211
The only issue we have is
that your tip picked up a bend

00:02:58.277 --> 00:03:00.246
when it chopped into the spine.

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:02.882
But, your weapon,
sir, will KEAL.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:04.584
 Thank you.

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:06.252
[ominous music playing]

00:03:06.319 --> 00:03:08.754
 All right, gentlemen, it's
time for the strength test.

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:12.124
Now, Attila's armies were
basically one large cavalry.

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:13.659
And through his
military campaigns,

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:16.596
he revolutionized the use of
horse in military conflicts.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:19.032
So to test the strength and
durability of your blades,

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:21.667
I'll be chopping into
these horse skulls.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.602
 Randy, you're up
first, are you ready?

00:03:23.669 --> 00:03:24.603
 I guess so.

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:25.971
[music playing]

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:29.609
[chopping]

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:33.213
[music playing]

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:38.618
[shattering]

00:03:40.986 --> 00:03:42.955
 Wow.

00:03:43.022 --> 00:03:44.223
 OK.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.693
So right off the bat,
the biggest thing

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:51.731
is that this section from
right about here, to here,

00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:53.499
has lost its edge.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:59.204
There's a couple of small
rolls, plate's still straight,

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:00.773
it's all in one
piece, still solid.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.508
Nicely done, it's a
very strong blade.

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:03.175
 Thank you.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.043
 All right, Dan.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:04.943
Are you ready?

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:05.678
 No, but let's do it.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:06.379
[laughter]

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:08.147
 Everybody says that.

00:04:08.214 --> 00:04:10.683
[music playing]

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:14.053
[chopping]

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.657
[music playing]

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:22.495
[clanging]

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:23.930
 Oh, wow.

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:28.935
At the guard.

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:35.207
 OK.

00:04:35.307 --> 00:04:37.510
So before we get to
the obvious, I really

00:04:37.576 --> 00:04:39.578
like the design of your blade.

00:04:39.679 --> 00:04:41.380
It's got a great
weight to it, had

00:04:41.446 --> 00:04:42.782
a really good feel in my hand.

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.750
The balance was really nice.

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.953
See all that space
around your tang?

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:51.657
With that room for that blade
to move inside the guard,

00:04:51.724 --> 00:04:55.428
it could just create so much
stress that it cut loose

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:56.896
right there at the corner.

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:59.465
If it were all tight, there
wouldn't be any stress.

00:04:59.532 --> 00:05:01.967
There's no discoloration
here, so it's not that there

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:03.269
was a crack here before.

00:05:03.335 --> 00:05:04.703
The grain structure looks fine.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:09.108
It was a well designed
piece, but obvious flaw.

00:05:09.175 --> 00:05:10.676
[music playing]

00:05:10.776 --> 00:05:13.112
 Dan, unfortunately, your blade
suffered a catastrophic failure

00:05:13.179 --> 00:05:14.780
in the middle of
our strength test,

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:17.649
which means that we
can no longer test it.

00:05:17.749 --> 00:05:19.719
I'd like to invite you
to shake our hands,

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:22.020
shake your competitor's
hand, and then

00:05:22.087 --> 00:05:23.389
please leave the Forge.

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:26.125
 It hurts, but my
sword breaking, it's

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:27.293
going to be a
reminder that I have

00:05:27.359 --> 00:05:28.694
to push harder and be better.

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:32.231
 Randy, the strength and
efficiency of your weapon

00:05:32.297 --> 00:05:33.766
in the KEAL test have
earned you the title

00:05:33.833 --> 00:05:36.969
of Forged in Fire Champion,
and a check for how much?

00:05:37.036 --> 00:05:37.903
 $10,000.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.338
 That's right, $10,000.

00:05:39.438 --> 00:05:40.272
Good job, brother.

00:05:40.339 --> 00:05:41.841
 I won "Forged in Fire."

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:42.675
It's reality.

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:43.742
 How do you feel?

00:05:43.842 --> 00:05:45.078
 Good.

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:48.381
To be a champion and be
recognized as a good bladesmith

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:50.282
is real good.

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.884
This is my happy
and excited face.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:53.719
 Well done, sir.

00:05:53.786 --> 00:05:54.519
 Thank you.

00:05:54.586 --> 00:05:55.388
If you didn't recognize it.

00:05:55.455 --> 00:05:58.991
[music playing]

00:05:59.792 --> 00:06:00.493
[clang]

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.830
 Jason, Don, congratulations.

00:06:04.897 --> 00:06:07.699
You've made it into the third
round of this competition.

00:06:07.799 --> 00:06:09.669
We're sending you back
to your home forges

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:12.872
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:17.743
That weapon is, The Scissor.

00:06:17.810 --> 00:06:18.344
[laughter]

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:19.278
 Oh, God.

00:06:19.345 --> 00:06:20.713
 Oh, God.

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.715
NARRATOR: Wielded by
gladiators in ancient Rome,

00:06:22.781 --> 00:06:25.351
the Scissor was an ideal weapon
for the bloody battles that

00:06:25.417 --> 00:06:27.220
ensued in the Colosseum arena.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.455
The contour of the sharp
crescent shaped blade

00:06:29.521 --> 00:06:31.524
was optimal for
slashing and stabbing,

00:06:31.624 --> 00:06:34.627
while the armor encasing the
forearm offered protection.

00:06:34.727 --> 00:06:37.864
Gladiators who use the scissor
were also known as Scissores.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:40.632
It could swiftly brandish the
weapon in the heat of battle

00:06:40.699 --> 00:06:42.568
due to its surprisingly
lightweight.

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:45.471
The dual blocking cut
capabilities of the scissor

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:48.508
freed the users other arm
for another weapon or shield,

00:06:48.574 --> 00:06:51.343
giving the user the advantage
of multiple ways to attack.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:52.311
 All right, gentlemen.

00:06:52.411 --> 00:06:53.546
This is the sharpness test.

00:06:53.612 --> 00:06:55.447
To test the sharpness
of your edge,

00:06:55.514 --> 00:06:57.516
I'm going to attack our
Sandman here several times.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.518
We'll see how they do.

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:00.519
Jason, you're up first.

00:07:00.586 --> 00:07:01.320
Are you ready for this?

00:07:01.387 --> 00:07:02.254
 Yes, sir.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:05.057
 All right, let's do it.

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:05.791
[music playing]

00:07:05.858 --> 00:07:08.794
[slashing]

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:12.432
[music playing]

00:07:17.236 --> 00:07:18.070
[laughter]

00:07:18.170 --> 00:07:19.438
 All right.

00:07:19.504 --> 00:07:21.207
The handle feels
really good in my hand,

00:07:21.273 --> 00:07:25.777
but the shape of your blade,
not being as deep a crescent,

00:07:25.877 --> 00:07:28.414
made it a little bit
more difficult to slash.

00:07:28.481 --> 00:07:31.483
All in all, solid, and
it's got a good look.

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:32.250
Nicely done.

00:07:32.317 --> 00:07:33.085
 Thank you.

00:07:33.152 --> 00:07:33.819
 All right, Don.

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:34.353
You ready?

00:07:34.453 --> 00:07:36.155
 I'm ready.

00:07:36.222 --> 00:07:37.757
[music playing]

00:07:37.857 --> 00:07:41.127
[slashing]

00:07:41.194 --> 00:07:44.730
[music playing]

00:07:54.239 --> 00:07:58.577
 Don, I like the way this is
set up tighter around the arm.

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:01.380
Right here at my
hand, my knuckle

00:08:01.480 --> 00:08:03.982
is just pounding into the side.

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.752
You can see it slashed
pretty easily on the arm.

00:08:06.819 --> 00:08:10.255
And then on the forward
punch, didn't quite get

00:08:10.322 --> 00:08:12.324
the slash I was looking for.

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:13.892
All in all, though, did the job.

00:08:13.959 --> 00:08:14.827
 Thank you.

00:08:14.894 --> 00:08:16.162
 Next up, I'll
give you to Doug.

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:18.731
 Bladesmiths, this
is a KEAL test.

00:08:18.831 --> 00:08:21.200
To see what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:23.736
I will take your Scissor
and I will deliver killing

00:08:23.802 --> 00:08:26.172
blows on this ballistics dummy.

00:08:26.239 --> 00:08:27.305
Jason, you're up first.
You ready?

00:08:27.406 --> 00:08:28.173
 Let's do it.

00:08:28.274 --> 00:08:29.875
 Let's do this.

00:08:29.942 --> 00:08:33.513
[music playing]

00:08:34.313 --> 00:08:37.884
[chopping]

00:08:43.222 --> 00:08:44.590
[laughter]

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:47.259
 First off, the minute I
put my hand in your handle,

00:08:47.326 --> 00:08:52.598
it's not directly in line with
my fist, so it's slightly off.

00:08:52.665 --> 00:08:55.167
But as you can see, I can
still wield the weapon.

00:08:55.234 --> 00:08:59.605
The laceration was deep
into this cavity right here,

00:08:59.672 --> 00:09:01.707
so you've got a
very sharp blade.

00:09:01.774 --> 00:09:04.643
The hook you have penetrated
right into the heart

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.044
on the back hand draw.

00:09:06.144 --> 00:09:10.950
It lacerates and guts
everything out, and disembowel

00:09:11.050 --> 00:09:13.052
this ballistics dummy.

00:09:13.152 --> 00:09:15.921
Your weapon, sir, will KEAL.

00:09:15.988 --> 00:09:16.488
Good job, sir.

00:09:16.555 --> 00:09:17.255
 Thank you.

00:09:17.322 --> 00:09:18.457
 Don.

00:09:18.524 --> 00:09:19.358
Your turn.

00:09:19.425 --> 00:09:20.225
 Let's have some fun.

00:09:20.326 --> 00:09:21.527
 Let's do this.

00:09:21.594 --> 00:09:23.128
[music playing]

00:09:23.195 --> 00:09:26.465
[chopping]

00:09:26.532 --> 00:09:28.400
[music playing]

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:31.304
[laughter]

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:32.905
 Good.

00:09:32.972 --> 00:09:35.074
 Don, let's talk
about your weapon.

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:37.275
What I like about your
weapon is that it's

00:09:37.342 --> 00:09:38.944
in line with the handle.

00:09:39.010 --> 00:09:42.481
On the initial cut here, it
lacerated right through there.

00:09:42.581 --> 00:09:44.749
And in this back
hand hook, your edge

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:49.254
is deep to go in here and
right into that cavity.

00:09:49.321 --> 00:09:50.422
Your weapon will KEAL.

00:09:50.522 --> 00:09:51.657
 Thank you.

00:09:51.723 --> 00:09:52.657
 I think we're
running neck and neck,

00:09:52.724 --> 00:09:54.025
and it feels pretty amazing.

00:09:54.126 --> 00:09:55.928
But of course, I wish I
was further ahead of Don.

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:58.563
I wish his would just
spontaneously explode.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:09:59.598
 All right, gentlemen.

00:09:59.698 --> 00:10:00.966
This is the strength test.

00:10:01.066 --> 00:10:03.502
Now the Scissor was used
in gladiatorial combat

00:10:03.602 --> 00:10:05.304
for both attack and defense.

00:10:05.371 --> 00:10:07.973
Now to test the strength and
durability of your weapon,

00:10:08.074 --> 00:10:10.943
we'll clamp them into our
mechanical device here.

00:10:11.009 --> 00:10:14.179
The blade's going to come down
and strike the armored cuff

00:10:14.246 --> 00:10:15.314
of your weapon twice.

00:10:15.381 --> 00:10:16.448
And then your weapon
is going to be

00:10:16.514 --> 00:10:17.949
launched into this breastplate.

00:10:18.049 --> 00:10:19.652
Jason, I've already
got you're strapped in.

00:10:19.752 --> 00:10:21.120
You ready to go?
- Let's do it.

00:10:21.187 --> 00:10:21.921
 OK.

00:10:21.988 --> 00:10:22.921
[music playing]

00:10:22.988 --> 00:10:25.658
[clanging]

00:10:25.725 --> 00:10:27.893
[music playing]

00:10:38.871 --> 00:10:41.774
 Just the slightest roll.

00:10:41.874 --> 00:10:44.243
It's not deformed
beyond being sharp.

00:10:44.309 --> 00:10:48.147
And then you can see where the
sword came down and hit it.

00:10:48.247 --> 00:10:49.749
Caused a bit of deformation.

00:10:49.849 --> 00:10:53.251
And then, I think we were pushed
just a little further offline.

00:10:53.351 --> 00:10:58.123
Right in here, it looks like
it kind of waffled just a bit.

00:10:58.223 --> 00:11:01.360
But everything is still
tight, still sharp.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:02.160
Nicely done.

00:11:02.227 --> 00:11:02.895
 Thank you.

00:11:02.962 --> 00:11:03.962
 So, Don.

00:11:04.029 --> 00:11:04.496
You ready?

00:11:04.596 --> 00:11:05.731
 I'm ready.

00:11:05.831 --> 00:11:07.032
 All right, let's
get you strapped in.

00:11:07.099 --> 00:11:08.067
[laughter]

00:11:08.134 --> 00:11:11.737
[music playing]

00:11:12.504 --> 00:11:16.075
[clanging]

00:11:16.142 --> 00:11:19.679
[music playing]

00:11:22.314 --> 00:11:25.651
 So looking at this,
I'm having a hard time

00:11:25.717 --> 00:11:27.585
finding where the sword hit it.

00:11:27.686 --> 00:11:30.889
And there's one
teeny little mark.

00:11:30.989 --> 00:11:33.125
You know, blade
still tight, on that

00:11:33.192 --> 00:11:36.128
edge is still a razor blade,
there's no rolling at all.

00:11:36.195 --> 00:11:37.195
Very well done.

00:11:37.262 --> 00:11:38.096
It's nice.

00:11:38.163 --> 00:11:40.099
 Thank you.

00:11:40.166 --> 00:11:42.101
[music playing]

00:11:42.168 --> 00:11:43.969
 Bladesmiths,
you've worked very

00:11:44.035 --> 00:11:46.672
hard to recreate
weapons that we've never

00:11:46.738 --> 00:11:48.541
seen here in the Forge before.

00:11:48.607 --> 00:11:50.342
However, in this
competition, there can only

00:11:50.408 --> 00:11:52.578
be one Forged in Fire Champion.

00:11:52.678 --> 00:11:59.284
And that champion is Don.

00:11:59.351 --> 00:12:01.854
Congratulations, you are
the Forged in Fire Champion.

00:12:01.954 --> 00:12:03.022
 Yeah.

00:12:03.122 --> 00:12:04.389
Thank you.

00:12:04.456 --> 00:12:06.491
 Jason, unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:12:06.591 --> 00:12:08.493
Please surrender your Scissor.

00:12:08.594 --> 00:12:10.329
 I spent five days
making something

00:12:10.429 --> 00:12:11.864
I've never made before.

00:12:11.931 --> 00:12:14.499
I went up against a guy who
builds armor quite often.

00:12:14.566 --> 00:12:15.701
I held my own against him.

00:12:15.767 --> 00:12:17.736
I'm pretty proud of that fact.

00:12:17.803 --> 00:12:20.672
I loved every minute
of this experience.

00:12:20.772 --> 00:12:22.374
 Don, congratulations.

00:12:22.475 --> 00:12:23.742
You are the Forged
in Fire Champion

00:12:23.809 --> 00:12:26.845
and will be receiving
that check for $10,000.

00:12:26.912 --> 00:12:28.114
How do you feel right now?

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:29.248
 I feel fantastic.

00:12:29.348 --> 00:12:32.117
It feels great to be a
Forged in Fire Champion.

00:12:32.184 --> 00:12:33.252
$10,000.

00:12:33.352 --> 00:12:35.020
I'd like to get something
nice for my wife.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:37.555
We kind of had a little fun
making jokes at each other

00:12:37.622 --> 00:12:38.890
about Texas versus Oklahoma.

00:12:38.957 --> 00:12:41.060
Yeah, I'm glad to see
Texas came out on top.

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:41.994
[laughter]

00:12:42.061 --> 00:12:42.527
Woo!

00:12:42.594 --> 00:12:44.163
[laughter]

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:45.898
[music playing]

00:12:45.998 --> 00:12:46.766
[clang]

00:12:48.567 --> 00:12:49.467
[cymbals rolling]

00:12:49.534 --> 00:12:50.468
 Ooh.

00:12:50.535 --> 00:12:52.037
 The Egyptian Khopesh.

00:12:52.137 --> 00:12:53.671
 Cool.

00:12:53.772 --> 00:12:56.175
NARRATOR: Dating
back to 2,500 BC,

00:12:56.275 --> 00:12:59.845
the Khopesh was a curved sickle
sword adopted by Egyptians

00:12:59.912 --> 00:13:01.413
from the Canaanite.

00:13:01.479 --> 00:13:04.784
It was used to execute their
enemies as an infantry weapon,

00:13:04.884 --> 00:13:08.053
and also as a symbol of the
authority of their nobles.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:09.989
The unique shape of
their curved blades

00:13:10.055 --> 00:13:12.958
meant they could be used to
hook a shield, snag opponent's

00:13:13.025 --> 00:13:15.394
leg in an attempt to
trip them, or even

00:13:15.494 --> 00:13:17.596
tangle an opposing weapon.

00:13:17.663 --> 00:13:19.298
The weapon's
distinctive design makes

00:13:19.398 --> 00:13:22.100
the Khopesh easily
recognizable in television

00:13:22.201 --> 00:13:24.436
series such as
"Game of Thrones."

00:13:24.503 --> 00:13:27.138
 Bladesmiths, it is said
that the historic design

00:13:27.205 --> 00:13:29.408
of the Khopesh evolved
from a battle ax.

00:13:29.475 --> 00:13:31.710
Its edge was so sharp that
it is said it could cut

00:13:31.810 --> 00:13:32.945
through just about anything.

00:13:33.011 --> 00:13:34.880
To test the sharpness
of your weapon,

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.683
we'll see how well it
cuts through a sandbag,

00:13:37.783 --> 00:13:39.585
sugar cane, and a rope.

00:13:39.651 --> 00:13:40.452
 Salem, you're up.

00:13:40.519 --> 00:13:41.186
You ready?

00:13:41.253 --> 00:13:42.087
 Yes sir.

00:13:42.188 --> 00:13:44.122
[music playing]

00:13:44.189 --> 00:13:47.492
[hacking]

00:13:47.593 --> 00:13:49.161
[music playing]

00:13:51.963 --> 00:13:54.132
 Well, Salem, it
definitely is easy enough

00:13:54.233 --> 00:13:57.035
to cut through a sandbag,
cut through sugar cane.

00:13:57.102 --> 00:13:59.604
But the forward weight
being a little bit tip heavy

00:13:59.671 --> 00:14:02.240
was a little bit harder to slice
through on the upward stroke.

00:14:02.307 --> 00:14:05.444
But definitely, it's
a very sharp weapon.

00:14:05.511 --> 00:14:07.079
This, sir, will cut.

00:14:07.146 --> 00:14:07.679
Good job.

00:14:07.746 --> 00:14:08.547
 Thanks.

00:14:08.647 --> 00:14:09.548
 Craig you're up.

00:14:09.648 --> 00:14:10.348
You ready?

00:14:10.415 --> 00:14:12.751
 Yes, sir.

00:14:12.818 --> 00:14:14.352
[music playing]

00:14:14.419 --> 00:14:17.990
[hacking]

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:23.161
[music playing]

00:14:23.228 --> 00:14:27.132
 I'm just disappointed that
it wouldn't cut the rope.

00:14:27.199 --> 00:14:30.202
 Well, Craig, it cut
through a sandbag,

00:14:30.269 --> 00:14:33.471
cut all the way through three
sugar canes, but the same idea.

00:14:33.538 --> 00:14:36.875
On an upward swing for the
test, it did lacerate the rope,

00:14:36.975 --> 00:14:38.777
but it didn't cut through.

00:14:38.844 --> 00:14:42.681
But overall, it will cut.

00:14:42.781 --> 00:14:45.985
Now it's time to move
on to the KEAL test.

00:14:46.085 --> 00:14:48.420
To test the functionality
and lethality of your blade,

00:14:48.487 --> 00:14:51.590
I will attempt to rip off the
shields, then deliver killing

00:14:51.656 --> 00:14:53.258
blows on this ballistic dummy.

00:14:53.325 --> 00:14:55.561
Let's see how much damage
your weapon can do.

00:14:55.628 --> 00:14:56.394
Salem you're up.

00:14:56.461 --> 00:14:57.162
You ready?

00:14:57.229 --> 00:14:57.729
 All right.

00:14:57.796 --> 00:14:58.697
[music playing]

00:14:58.797 --> 00:15:00.732
[thud]

00:15:00.832 --> 00:15:02.734
[slicing]

00:15:02.801 --> 00:15:04.336
[music playing]

00:15:04.436 --> 00:15:06.405
[chopping]

00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:12.644
 The hook on your tip does
allow to rip off the shield.

00:15:12.711 --> 00:15:15.547
The edge you have right here
caused some serious damage.

00:15:18.183 --> 00:15:20.519
Enough to cut all the way
through the belly here.

00:15:20.586 --> 00:15:23.922
At the same time, I've cut
through all these bones,

00:15:23.988 --> 00:15:26.258
from the clavicle,
through the ribs.

00:15:28.694 --> 00:15:30.663
This sir, KEAL.

00:15:33.064 --> 00:15:33.999
Craig, it's your turn.

00:15:34.066 --> 00:15:34.766
Are you ready?

00:15:34.833 --> 00:15:35.466
 Yes sir.

00:15:35.567 --> 00:15:36.334
 Let's do this.

00:15:36.435 --> 00:15:39.638
[music playing]

00:15:39.738 --> 00:15:43.208
[slicing]

00:15:43.976 --> 00:15:46.078
[chopping]

00:15:47.679 --> 00:15:51.149
 Well, Craig, what I like
about your particular hook

00:15:51.216 --> 00:15:55.253
design over here is that as you
puncture, twist, and rip out,

00:15:55.354 --> 00:15:56.788
everything that
you have in there

00:15:56.854 --> 00:15:58.857
will hook and come out with it.

00:15:58.924 --> 00:16:01.860
The edge cut all the
way into the bone

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:03.962
and broke these ribs to sternum.

00:16:04.062 --> 00:16:06.331
This sir, will KEAL.

00:16:06.431 --> 00:16:07.566
 Thank you.

00:16:07.666 --> 00:16:09.501
 Next up is a strength test.

00:16:09.601 --> 00:16:10.602
Dave.

00:16:10.702 --> 00:16:11.903
 Gentlemen, what
I'm going to do

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:13.672
to test the strength
of your weapons

00:16:13.739 --> 00:16:16.875
is take seven blows against
these animal femurs.

00:16:16.941 --> 00:16:17.809
Salem, you're up.

00:16:17.876 --> 00:16:18.610
Are you ready?

00:16:18.677 --> 00:16:19.845
 Great.

00:16:19.911 --> 00:16:22.113
 Now Salem, in
examining your weapon,

00:16:22.180 --> 00:16:26.618 line:8%
we noticed a small delamination
on the back of the blade.

00:16:26.685 --> 00:16:28.153 line:14%
 I was not expecting that.

00:16:28.220 --> 00:16:30.255 line:8%
I'm just hoping that
the edge stays hard.

00:16:30.355 --> 00:16:33.292 line:8%
 So we're going to keep an eye
on that through the testing,

00:16:33.358 --> 00:16:35.627
and we'll see if it opens up.

00:16:35.694 --> 00:16:36.628
[chopping]

00:16:36.695 --> 00:16:37.629
[music playing]

00:16:37.696 --> 00:16:40.932
[chopping]

00:16:41.033 --> 00:16:44.603
[music playing]

00:16:47.572 --> 00:16:48.841
[sighs]

00:16:48.941 --> 00:16:52.644
 Well, Salem, that did
a job on those bones.

00:16:52.744 --> 00:16:55.313
Now, there's a little bit
of deflection on your blade,

00:16:55.414 --> 00:16:59.250
but that back mark didn't
open or split at all.

00:16:59.317 --> 00:17:02.654
Now you can see, I went
through two of those bones,

00:17:02.754 --> 00:17:04.923
and was well into the third.

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:05.690
Well done.

00:17:05.757 --> 00:17:06.658
 Thank you.

00:17:06.725 --> 00:17:08.393
 So Craig, it's your turn.

00:17:08.460 --> 00:17:08.960
You ready?

00:17:09.027 --> 00:17:09.928
 Let's do it.

00:17:10.028 --> 00:17:11.596
 All right.

00:17:11.663 --> 00:17:13.999
[music playing]

00:17:14.099 --> 00:17:17.568
[chopping]

00:17:17.669 --> 00:17:20.939
[music playing]

00:17:21.006 --> 00:17:24.576
[hacking]

00:17:24.643 --> 00:17:26.645
[music playing]

00:17:28.613 --> 00:17:30.949
[exhaling]

00:17:31.016 --> 00:17:34.620
 Well, Craig, you
can see a lot of chips

00:17:34.686 --> 00:17:36.988
right there in the impact zone.

00:17:37.055 --> 00:17:38.623
The first few
blows against those

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:41.160
femurs, it started
cutting really nicely.

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:44.195 line:8%
Broke through the one, but as
we started to lose edge here,

00:17:44.262 --> 00:17:46.198 line:8%
what those chips
and deflections,

00:17:46.264 --> 00:17:47.899 line:8%
it just stopped
cutting, and it was more

00:17:47.965 --> 00:17:51.269
of a bludgeoning impact blow.

00:17:51.336 --> 00:17:54.873
But I felt it really cut
well when I was swinging it.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:56.708
All in all, nice design.

00:17:56.774 --> 00:17:58.310
I like your handle construction.

00:17:58.376 --> 00:18:00.912
And it's definitely a chopper.

00:18:00.979 --> 00:18:04.616
So gentlemen, good job.

00:18:04.683 --> 00:18:06.885
[music playing]

00:18:06.952 --> 00:18:08.586
 Salem, Craig.

00:18:08.653 --> 00:18:11.356
There can only be one
Forged in Fire Champion.

00:18:16.728 --> 00:18:20.532
Salem, you are the Forged in
Fire Champion, congratulations.

00:18:20.599 --> 00:18:21.466
[music playing]

00:18:21.533 --> 00:18:22.500
 Good job.

00:18:22.567 --> 00:18:23.235
 Thank you.

00:18:23.335 --> 00:18:25.170
Good job to you, too.

00:18:25.237 --> 00:18:29.140
 Craig, unfortunately, your
blade did not make the cut.

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:30.476
Please surrender your weapon.

00:18:33.078 --> 00:18:34.613
 All right, thank you.

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:38.517
This experience was harder than
I thought it was going to be.

00:18:38.584 --> 00:18:40.518
I need about three
gin and tonics.

00:18:40.585 --> 00:18:42.887
And I'm just going to make the
bad man in the back of my head

00:18:42.954 --> 00:18:43.622
go away.

00:18:43.689 --> 00:18:44.923
[music playing]

00:18:45.023 --> 00:18:47.526
 Salem, it's safe to
smile now because you're

00:18:47.593 --> 00:18:50.795
the Forged in Fire Champion,
the recipient of $10,000.

00:18:50.896 --> 00:18:51.563
Congratulations.

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:54.499
[applause]

00:18:54.566 --> 00:18:59.036
 The fullers on that blade just
really bring that pattern out.

00:18:59.137 --> 00:19:00.739
I think that's
really nice touch.

00:19:00.806 --> 00:19:03.075
 That's just crazy.

00:19:03.175 --> 00:19:05.243
It's going to take
a while to sink in.

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:06.511
Kind of stunned right now.

00:19:06.578 --> 00:19:09.681
[music playing]

00:19:09.781 --> 00:19:10.549
[clang]

00:19:12.984 --> 00:19:16.154
NARRATOR: The Roman Gladius.

00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:18.756
The word gladius
means sword in Latin.

00:19:18.823 --> 00:19:21.292
It was also adopted as the
name for those who would fight

00:19:21.359 --> 00:19:23.261
each other to the death
for the entertainment

00:19:23.361 --> 00:19:25.930
of the imperial crowns, as
depicted in the Hollywood

00:19:25.997 --> 00:19:27.966
blockbuster, "Gladiator."

00:19:28.066 --> 00:19:31.436
The gladius was the primary
weapon of the Roman legionary,

00:19:31.536 --> 00:19:34.572
with a fearsome V-shaped tip
for thrusting and stabbing,

00:19:34.639 --> 00:19:38.776
and a double razor sharp edge
for slashing and slicing.

00:19:38.843 --> 00:19:42.014
Originally a Spanish weapon,
the Romans were so impressed

00:19:42.114 --> 00:19:44.515
by its simple design and
lethal effectiveness,

00:19:44.615 --> 00:19:46.818
they adopted it as
their own and used

00:19:46.918 --> 00:19:49.921
it to help them establish
one of the greatest empires

00:19:50.021 --> 00:19:51.823
the world has ever known.

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:54.359
 With a slice test, I
will take your weapon

00:19:54.426 --> 00:19:57.261
and slash through branches,
vines, and sugar cane.

00:19:57.361 --> 00:19:59.864
So different layers,
different consistencies.

00:19:59.931 --> 00:20:00.999
Jamie, you're up first.

00:20:01.066 --> 00:20:01.766
Are you ready?

00:20:01.833 --> 00:20:02.501
 I am.

00:20:02.601 --> 00:20:04.769
[chopping]

00:20:04.836 --> 00:20:05.770
[music playing]

00:20:05.837 --> 00:20:08.707
[slashing]

00:20:08.774 --> 00:20:12.311
[music playing]

00:20:16.381 --> 00:20:18.683
 Definitely a
good impact weapon.

00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:22.087
Only thing was, at the end,
as you're doing more shots,

00:20:22.154 --> 00:20:24.856
it starts to rotate with
a very rounded handle.

00:20:24.923 --> 00:20:30.528
But it is sharp, and for
this test, it can cut.

00:20:30.629 --> 00:20:31.996
Mareko, you're up next.
You ready?

00:20:32.096 --> 00:20:32.763
 I'm ready.

00:20:32.864 --> 00:20:34.199
[music playing]

00:20:34.266 --> 00:20:37.769
[slashing]

00:20:37.836 --> 00:20:41.005
[music playing]

00:20:41.072 --> 00:20:41.840
[clang]

00:20:46.745 --> 00:20:49.046
 Very light on the hand.

00:20:49.113 --> 00:20:50.615
Very sharp.

00:20:50.715 --> 00:20:54.286
A lot of the sugar canes have
very clean cuts despite being

00:20:54.352 --> 00:20:56.221
surrounded by these branches.

00:20:56.288 --> 00:20:59.891
The handle construction
felt secure in my hand.

00:20:59.991 --> 00:21:00.959
It will cut.

00:21:01.026 --> 00:21:01.793
Good job.

00:21:01.893 --> 00:21:03.395
 Thank you very much.

00:21:03.462 --> 00:21:05.463
 Now it's time
for the KEAL test.

00:21:05.563 --> 00:21:07.365
To test the lethality
of your weapon,

00:21:07.466 --> 00:21:10.501
I will slash, cut, and
stab this ballistics dummy

00:21:10.568 --> 00:21:13.939
that is dressed like a
Gladiator in the Roman era.

00:21:14.006 --> 00:21:15.172
Jamie, you're up.
Are you ready?

00:21:15.239 --> 00:21:15.941
 Absolutely.

00:21:16.008 --> 00:21:19.278
[music playing]

00:21:22.681 --> 00:21:26.051
[slashing]

00:21:29.021 --> 00:21:32.524
[music playing]

00:21:32.591 --> 00:21:33.925
[stabbing]

00:21:33.992 --> 00:21:36.561
[music playing]

00:21:39.164 --> 00:21:42.233
 Well, that lacerated all
the way through to the bone.

00:21:42.333 --> 00:21:45.337
Destroyed the
clavicle completely.

00:21:45.403 --> 00:21:47.972
Disemboweled here.

00:21:48.039 --> 00:21:50.742
Thrust went through.

00:21:50.842 --> 00:21:52.343
And that's definitely
a kill shot

00:21:52.443 --> 00:21:55.146
all the way into the spine.

00:21:55.213 --> 00:21:57.282
This will KEAL.

00:21:57.382 --> 00:21:58.082
Good job.

00:21:58.149 --> 00:21:59.784
 Thank you.

00:21:59.884 --> 00:22:00.952
 Mareko, you're next.

00:22:01.019 --> 00:22:01.686
You ready?

00:22:01.786 --> 00:22:02.754
 I'm ready.

00:22:02.821 --> 00:22:04.155
[music playing]

00:22:04.255 --> 00:22:07.726
[slicing]

00:22:07.793 --> 00:22:08.693
[music playing]

00:22:08.760 --> 00:22:10.095
[stabbing]

00:22:10.162 --> 00:22:13.699
[music playing]

00:22:16.635 --> 00:22:18.603
[stabbing]

00:22:19.971 --> 00:22:20.872
[music playing]

00:22:20.939 --> 00:22:23.341
 That's all the way through.

00:22:23.441 --> 00:22:25.643
Disemboweled on that pass.

00:22:25.744 --> 00:22:29.247
Throat, all the
way to the spine.

00:22:29.314 --> 00:22:30.982
It will KEAL.

00:22:31.049 --> 00:22:31.749
Good job.

00:22:31.816 --> 00:22:34.219
 Thank you.

00:22:34.285 --> 00:22:36.421
 Now to test the
strength of your weapon,

00:22:36.488 --> 00:22:40.425
your gladius will be placed
on this dynamic testing rig.

00:22:40.492 --> 00:22:42.494
This rig is
calibrated to deliver

00:22:42.594 --> 00:22:46.231
a strong blow similar to a
Roman legionnaire from his era.

00:22:46.297 --> 00:22:48.333
Your gladius will
strike our gladius

00:22:48.433 --> 00:22:52.037
that is made of 1055 high
carbon steel, three times,

00:22:52.104 --> 00:22:55.640
or until one of
the blades break.

00:22:55.706 --> 00:22:58.443
Jamie, your gladius is
already loaded into this rig.

00:22:58.510 --> 00:22:59.210
Are you ready?

00:22:59.277 --> 00:23:00.044
 I am.

00:23:00.111 --> 00:23:03.648
 In 3, 2, 1, engage!

00:23:03.715 --> 00:23:05.050
[clattering]

00:23:05.117 --> 00:23:08.520
[music playing]

00:23:09.153 --> 00:23:09.954
 Engage!

00:23:10.054 --> 00:23:10.922
[clattering]

00:23:13.224 --> 00:23:14.892
 Engage!

00:23:14.959 --> 00:23:15.927
[clattering]

00:23:19.164 --> 00:23:21.433
[music playing]

00:23:21.499 --> 00:23:24.602
 Well, your edge held
all the way through.

00:23:24.702 --> 00:23:27.139
Little indentations
there, nothing major.

00:23:27.205 --> 00:23:28.673
This crushed right
through the sword,

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:31.108
so this would have
broken the soldier's arm.

00:23:31.175 --> 00:23:31.909
That's a strong sword.

00:23:31.976 --> 00:23:32.677
Good job.

00:23:32.744 --> 00:23:33.978
 Thank you.

00:23:34.078 --> 00:23:35.179
 OK, Mareko.

00:23:35.246 --> 00:23:36.080
You're up.

00:23:36.147 --> 00:23:37.482
 I'm ready.

00:23:37.549 --> 00:23:40.652
My biggest fear is that
it's going to make contact

00:23:40.718 --> 00:23:42.554
and it's just going to break.

00:23:42.654 --> 00:23:45.322
 In 3, 2, 1, engage!

00:23:45.389 --> 00:23:46.658
[clattering]

00:23:47.191 --> 00:23:48.192
 Engage!

00:23:48.292 --> 00:23:49.494
[clattering]

00:23:50.228 --> 00:23:53.197
 3, 2, 1, engage!

00:23:53.264 --> 00:23:54.433
[clattering]

00:23:57.101 --> 00:23:59.203
 It held up.

00:23:59.303 --> 00:24:01.439
More scratches to the blade.

00:24:01.539 --> 00:24:02.407
That is a strong blade, sir.

00:24:02.474 --> 00:24:03.308
Congratulations.

00:24:03.408 --> 00:24:05.810
 Thank you very much.

00:24:05.877 --> 00:24:06.578
 Jamie.

00:24:06.678 --> 00:24:08.213
Mareko.

00:24:08.279 --> 00:24:09.948
There can only be one champion.

00:24:14.218 --> 00:24:19.157
Jamie, you are the Forged in
Fire Champion, congratulations.

00:24:19.257 --> 00:24:20.492
 Thank you.

00:24:20.558 --> 00:24:23.628
 Mareko, your blade
did not make the cut.

00:24:23.728 --> 00:24:26.564
 Mareko, I honestly
love your sword,

00:24:26.630 --> 00:24:29.567
but functionality is the key.

00:24:29.668 --> 00:24:32.337
I just cannot overlook
that handle coming apart.

00:24:32.403 --> 00:24:35.006
 Mareko, please
surrender your weapon.

00:24:35.073 --> 00:24:36.841
 It definitely sucks.

00:24:36.907 --> 00:24:39.677
But it feels really good to
have had a chance to challenge

00:24:39.777 --> 00:24:43.047
myself, and to step
outside my comfort zone,

00:24:43.114 --> 00:24:44.448
and do a good job at it.

00:24:44.515 --> 00:24:46.251
 Jamie, congratulations.

00:24:46.351 --> 00:24:48.252
You'll be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:24:48.319 --> 00:24:49.654
 Thank you.

00:24:49.721 --> 00:24:51.255
 Do you feel like fortune
favored the [inaudible]

00:24:51.322 --> 00:24:52.690
 I do.

00:24:52.757 --> 00:24:54.392
I feel like I took some
chances, and those decisions

00:24:54.492 --> 00:24:55.627
help me win this competition.

00:24:55.693 --> 00:24:57.895
 For me, it's all
about the detail.

00:24:57.962 --> 00:25:00.531
The choice of materials,
the way you laid it out.

00:25:00.632 --> 00:25:02.333
This is really,
really nice work.

00:25:02.433 --> 00:25:03.268
 Thank you.

00:25:03.335 --> 00:25:04.435
 I feel good.

00:25:04.535 --> 00:25:07.405
It's $10,000,
definitely help me out.

00:25:07.506 --> 00:25:09.440
Maybe might find some
time for a little vacation

00:25:09.540 --> 00:25:10.474
somewhere here or there.

00:25:10.541 --> 00:25:11.876
We'll see, we'll see.

00:25:11.943 --> 00:25:13.278
[laughter]

00:25:13.345 --> 00:25:15.680
[music playing]

00:25:15.747 --> 00:25:16.515
[clang]

00:25:18.649 --> 00:25:22.287
NARRATOR: The Moro Kris.

00:25:22.353 --> 00:25:27.591
The Kris came into existence
around 1361 AD in the kingdom

00:25:27.658 --> 00:25:30.428
of Majapahit, East Java.

00:25:30.495 --> 00:25:32.497
Believed to be the
primary weapons wielded

00:25:32.597 --> 00:25:35.567
by Asian warriors, its
distinctive, wavy blade

00:25:35.634 --> 00:25:38.770
creates a wider wound during
combat, causing the victim

00:25:38.837 --> 00:25:40.805
to quickly bleed to death.

00:25:40.871 --> 00:25:42.840
The hilt is viewed
as a work of art,

00:25:42.907 --> 00:25:45.310
and is often carved
in meticulous detail

00:25:45.410 --> 00:25:48.279
from precious wood,
gold, or ivory.

00:25:48.345 --> 00:25:52.216
In popular culture, the Kris
can be seen in the video game

00:25:52.317 --> 00:25:53.317
"Mortal Kombat."

00:25:53.418 --> 00:25:55.153
 The unique design
of a Moro Kris

00:25:55.253 --> 00:25:59.557
is made more distinct by
its fluid, wave like edges.

00:25:59.657 --> 00:26:02.293
It can thrust, but
its primary purpose

00:26:02.393 --> 00:26:04.061
is slashing and chopping.

00:26:04.162 --> 00:26:06.498
To test your Kris's ability
to perform according

00:26:06.598 --> 00:26:09.600
to its ancient design,
I will use it to chop

00:26:09.700 --> 00:26:12.303
and slice against
these moving targets.

00:26:12.403 --> 00:26:13.103
Mace, you're up first.

00:26:13.204 --> 00:26:13.838
Are you ready?

00:26:13.938 --> 00:26:14.472
 Sure.

00:26:14.539 --> 00:26:17.776
[music playing]

00:26:20.078 --> 00:26:23.582
[chopping]

00:26:25.883 --> 00:26:27.885
 Nice.

00:26:27.985 --> 00:26:30.888
 Nice balance, nice recovery.

00:26:30.989 --> 00:26:33.357
Allows you to move
with the blade.

00:26:33.424 --> 00:26:34.124
Good job.

00:26:34.191 --> 00:26:35.126
 Thank you.

00:26:35.193 --> 00:26:35.860
Murray, you're next.

00:26:35.961 --> 00:26:36.427
Are you ready?

00:26:36.494 --> 00:26:37.228
 Certainly am.

00:26:37.295 --> 00:26:40.832
[music playing]

00:26:40.899 --> 00:26:44.269
[slashing]

00:26:47.639 --> 00:26:51.076
[music playing]

00:26:52.143 --> 00:26:54.712
 Well, Murray, the
balance of this blade

00:26:54.812 --> 00:26:58.282
allows me to chase an attack,
and will come with me.

00:26:58.349 --> 00:27:01.519
On the recovery to go to another
attack, it will stay with me.

00:27:01.619 --> 00:27:03.922
It doesn't go away from me.

00:27:03.989 --> 00:27:05.389
It will slice.

00:27:05.456 --> 00:27:06.156
Good job.

00:27:06.223 --> 00:27:07.726
 Thank you.

00:27:07.826 --> 00:27:10.228
 To test the lethality of your
Kris, I will take your weapon,

00:27:10.295 --> 00:27:13.530
and I'm going to strike
into this animal carcass.

00:27:13.631 --> 00:27:14.599
Mace, you're up first.
You ready?

00:27:14.699 --> 00:27:15.400
 Yes, sir.

00:27:15.467 --> 00:27:18.970
[music playing]

00:27:20.338 --> 00:27:21.139
[slicing]

00:27:21.706 --> 00:27:22.874
[exhaling]

00:27:24.609 --> 00:27:25.910
[music playing]

00:27:25.977 --> 00:27:29.147
 Well, it cut cleanly
through the spine,

00:27:29.213 --> 00:27:34.018
all the way through the meat,
in one big, sweeping slash.

00:27:34.085 --> 00:27:35.620
It will KEAL.

00:27:35.687 --> 00:27:36.454
Good job.

00:27:36.554 --> 00:27:37.488
 Thank you, very much.

00:27:37.555 --> 00:27:38.155
 Murray, you are up next.

00:27:38.222 --> 00:27:38.889
You ready?

00:27:38.956 --> 00:27:39.590
 Yeah.

00:27:39.657 --> 00:27:43.194
[music playing]

00:27:45.630 --> 00:27:46.798
[slicing]

00:27:48.633 --> 00:27:51.503
[music playing]

00:27:51.603 --> 00:27:54.872
 When cutting through,
there was a slight drag

00:27:54.939 --> 00:27:56.107
in the feel of the cut.

00:27:56.207 --> 00:27:58.576
But it did cut very
cleanly through.

00:27:58.676 --> 00:28:01.446
It's a very, very sharp blade.

00:28:01.513 --> 00:28:03.614
It will KEAL.

00:28:03.681 --> 00:28:06.184
Bamboo is a very
durable material.

00:28:06.251 --> 00:28:10.588
Ounce for ounce, it is stronger
than concrete, brick, or wood.

00:28:10.688 --> 00:28:12.023
To test the strength
of your Kris,

00:28:12.123 --> 00:28:14.659
I will deliver more strikes
into the bamboo to see

00:28:14.725 --> 00:28:17.094
how well your weapon stands up.

00:28:17.195 --> 00:28:17.729
Mace, you're up.

00:28:17.796 --> 00:28:21.265
[music playing]

00:28:21.332 --> 00:28:24.635
[chopping]

00:28:24.702 --> 00:28:27.605
[music playing]

00:28:27.672 --> 00:28:28.840
[clanging]

00:28:31.609 --> 00:28:35.180
[music playing]

00:28:37.582 --> 00:28:41.086
Well, no damage
to the blade, sir.

00:28:41.152 --> 00:28:42.286
It chopped nicely.

00:28:42.353 --> 00:28:44.722
But a couple of times
over there, it did

00:28:44.789 --> 00:28:47.258
want to fall out of my
hand, just because it's

00:28:47.325 --> 00:28:49.026
so heavy on the blade.

00:28:49.093 --> 00:28:52.229
But nonetheless, it looks
like your edge did hold up.

00:28:52.329 --> 00:28:53.264
 Excellent.

00:28:53.331 --> 00:28:54.231
 Murray, you're up next.

00:28:54.298 --> 00:28:54.999
You ready?

00:28:55.066 --> 00:28:55.532
 Yes, I am.

00:28:55.633 --> 00:28:59.137
[music playing]

00:29:00.571 --> 00:29:04.042
[clanging]

00:29:04.109 --> 00:29:07.445
[music playing]

00:29:07.512 --> 00:29:09.114
[clanging]

00:29:17.455 --> 00:29:18.756
[music playing]

00:29:18.823 --> 00:29:21.192
 OK, Murray, looks
like your blade edge

00:29:21.259 --> 00:29:22.794
held up with the chops.

00:29:22.860 --> 00:29:26.063
It almost clearly sliced
all the way through.

00:29:26.163 --> 00:29:27.665
But there is now
an issue that we're

00:29:27.765 --> 00:29:29.233
looking at with your blade.

00:29:29.333 --> 00:29:32.070
I think there might be a
little bend here caused

00:29:32.136 --> 00:29:34.472
from chopping into the bamboo.

00:29:34.539 --> 00:29:38.709
But other than that, still
has a very sharp edge.

00:29:38.776 --> 00:29:40.544
The strength of
the blade held up.

00:29:40.611 --> 00:29:41.311
Good job.

00:29:41.378 --> 00:29:42.146
 Thank you.

00:29:42.213 --> 00:29:45.149
[music playing]

00:29:45.216 --> 00:29:49.186
 Gentlemen, you have
both done immaculate work.

00:29:49.253 --> 00:29:58.696
However, in this Forge there can
only be one winner of $10,000.

00:29:58.796 --> 00:30:02.366
Mace, you are the
Forged in Fire Champion.

00:30:02.433 --> 00:30:03.234
 Yes!

00:30:03.334 --> 00:30:04.035
 Congratulations.

00:30:04.102 --> 00:30:05.002
[laughter]

00:30:05.102 --> 00:30:06.170
- Thank you, Murray.
- Nice job, man.

00:30:06.237 --> 00:30:07.906
- Thanks, very much.
- Happy for you.

00:30:08.006 --> 00:30:11.242
 Murray, unfortunately your
Kris did not make the cut.

00:30:11.309 --> 00:30:13.911
 Murray, I find that
weapon absolutely

00:30:13.978 --> 00:30:15.546
beautiful and comfortable.

00:30:15.612 --> 00:30:19.216
But the fact that there's a
soft core in there somewhere,

00:30:19.316 --> 00:30:23.454
and that it picked up a bend
where your opponent's blade did

00:30:23.555 --> 00:30:25.756
not, that was the
deciding factor,

00:30:25.856 --> 00:30:28.560
and that's why we
had to let you go.

00:30:28.626 --> 00:30:31.896
 Murray, please
surrender your weapon.

00:30:31.996 --> 00:30:34.064
 While there's
always disappointment

00:30:34.164 --> 00:30:36.634
when one puts their best
effort forward and doesn't win.

00:30:36.734 --> 00:30:37.501
 Thank you, gentlemen.

00:30:37.601 --> 00:30:38.903
 No, thank you, Murray.

00:30:39.003 --> 00:30:42.139
 I do feel an overwhelming
sense of gratitude

00:30:42.239 --> 00:30:44.442
for having been
able to participate.

00:30:44.542 --> 00:30:48.679
Mace made the better blade,
and I'm proud of him.

00:30:48.746 --> 00:30:50.614
 Mace, congratulations.

00:30:50.681 --> 00:30:51.782
 Woo!

00:30:51.883 --> 00:30:54.419
 It's fantastic.

00:30:54.485 --> 00:30:55.820
I mean, the steel is beautiful.

00:30:55.887 --> 00:30:58.222
I like how you did the
file-work on the blade.

00:30:58.322 --> 00:31:02.092
The blade held up beautifully,
the edge is razor sharp,

00:31:02.193 --> 00:31:04.395
you should be exceptionally
proud of that piece.

00:31:04.462 --> 00:31:05.629
You did a great job.

00:31:05.730 --> 00:31:07.631
 I'm the Forged
in Fire Champion.

00:31:07.698 --> 00:31:08.833
I feel good.

00:31:08.899 --> 00:31:10.635
And I'm glad it came out on top.

00:31:10.702 --> 00:31:11.402
I'm the Tiger.

00:31:11.469 --> 00:31:14.138
[music playing]

00:31:14.238 --> 00:31:15.238
[clang]

